The process in which a function calls itself directly or indirectly is called recursion

Steps to solve a problem using recursion:
1. Define a base case
2. Define a recursive case

When does Stack Overflow error occur in recursion? when recursion continues indefinitely
    If the base case is not reached or not defined,
    then the stack overflow problem may arise.

How memory is allocated to different function calls in recursion?
    Recursion uses more memory to store data of every recursive call in an internal function call stack
    That stack frame stores everything needed to continue the function later, including: The values of its local variables, Where to return after the function finishes.

ITERATIVE LL:
    head stays
    curr moves
       ↓
    you manually manage traversal


RECURSIVE LL:
    head changes between calls
       ↓
    call stack remembers previous heads
       ↓
    recursion processes the rest
       ↓
    current node handles the result


